# /auto_release_monitor/arm  --  start monitoring one hand for a human pull.
#
# Replaces std_srvs/Trigger, which had no request fields and so could not carry
# the session token. Without the token the orchestrator cannot tell a pull
# detected during THIS handover from one detected during an earlier handover and
# delivered late: the release request carries no origin time, so stamping its
# receipt time shows only when it arrived.
#
# ONE AUTHORITATIVE TOKEN. The orchestrator creates it (handover_state.
# new_session_token) once per arming, passes it here, and the monitor echoes
# that same value back in its release request. The monitor never generates one.
string side           # "left" or "right"; must match the monitor's own ~side
string session_token  # opaque, non-empty; echoed verbatim in the release request
---
bool   success
string message
# Echoed back so the caller can confirm the monitor stored the token it sent.
string session_token
